  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find a formula for the alternating sum of squares, $$1^2-2^2+\\cdots+(2n-1)^2-(2n)^2.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-n(2n+1)$.\n\nPair consecutive terms and factor each difference of squares.",
      "worked": "For the $k$th pair,\n$$\\begin{align*}(2k-1)^2-(2k)^2&=((2k-1)-2k)((2k-1)+2k)\\\\(2k-1)^2-(2k)^2&=-(4k-1).\n\\end{align*}$$\nLet $S=1^2-2^2+\\cdots+(2n-1)^2-(2n)^2$. There are $n$ pairs, so\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=-3-7-\\cdots-(4n-1)\\\\S&=-4(1+2+\\cdots+n)+n\\\\S&=-4\\left(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right)+n\\\\S&=-n(2n+1).\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
